.TH WERKMEISTER-INFRA-CONNECT 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-infra\-connect \- Start all shared infrastructure (local + k8s port\-forwards)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister infra connect\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-k8s\fR
Start/restart k8s port\-forwards container only (replaces standalone k8s\-connect command)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fB`\-\-k8s`\fR starts or checks only the containerized k8s port\-forwards. Starts the \fBk8s\-forwards\fR Docker container (part of \fBinfra/compose/shared\-infra.yml\fR) which runs all 12 \fBkubectl port\-forward\fR processes (9 application + 3 infrastructure) inside a single container. If the container is already running, the command checks its health status.
.PP
The container runs on the \fBwerkmeister\-shared\fR Docker network and is accessible to other containers via the DNS name \fBk8s\-forwards\fR. Port\-forward processes inside the container auto\-restart if they disconnect, managed by the container's entrypoint script.
.PP
After starting, it runs a health check and reports the status.
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[info] Starting k8s\-forwards container...
[ok]   k8s\-forwards container is healthy. 12/12 forwards active.
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
